  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X\\ge 6).$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(X\\ge 6).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $X\\ge 6,$ not $X>6.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $X\\ge 6$ to the form $X>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $X,$ we see that $X\\ge 6$ is equivalent to $X>4.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
